**Plan for the next change.** The algorithms in this course will not last forever. NIST IR 8547 (October 2026) sets the transition to post-quantum cryptography: RSA, finite-field Diffie-Hellman and elliptic-curve cryptography are deprecated after 2030 and disallowed after 2035, because a large quantum computer would break them. TLS is already moving to hybrid key exchange with ML-KEM (RFC 10024, covered in *TLS and PKI in practice*). Your code is ready for that kind of change if:

- each message or record carries a version and a key id, as in lesson 10;
- algorithms are chosen in configuration in one place, not scattered through code;
- you keep an inventory of keys, their algorithms, purposes, owners and rotation dates.
